name: BEX Program
description: >
  Blue Expression Object (BEX) program. A BEX Program is deterministic Blue data
  selected by a host for compilation and execution by a BEX engine. It may define
  constants, functions, an inline expression body, an ordered statement body, an
  entry function selector, execution flags, and a gas limit.

  BEX Program is not JavaScript, WASM, a network runtime, an LLM extension
  point, or a contract processor. It has no ambient time, randomness,
  filesystem, network, database, asynchronous execution, or hidden mutable
  state. Host capabilities are available only through explicitly registered
  intrinsic processors.

expr:
  description: Optional single BEX expression.
do:
  type: List
  description: Ordered BEX statement body.
definition:
  description: Optional reference to reusable BEX definitions.
entry:
  type: Text
  description: Entry function name.
constants:
  type: Dictionary
  description: Literal constants available through $const.
functions:
  type: Dictionary
  description: Local BEX function definitions keyed by function name.
emitEvents:
  type: Boolean
  description: Whether result events are emitted by the host.
returnResult:
  type: Boolean
  description: Whether the host retains the result.
gasLimit:
  type: Integer
  description: Optional maximum BEX gas.
